# [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_PROBE] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]

Parallel probe orchestration preserving input order.

## RUN_ALL

<!-- [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_PROBE] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]: fans out one goroutine per target and waits for all probes -->

Contract:
  INPUT: targets slice; parent context; timeout > 0; dialFn injectable for tests
  OUTPUT: results slice with len(results) == len(targets)
  DATA: results[] — one slot per target index
  PRE: len(targets) >= 1; timeout > 0
  POST: len(results) == len(targets); results[i] corresponds to targets[i]
  EFFECTS: Async; one concurrent worker per target; each worker applies per-probe deadline then AWAIT ATTEMPT_DIAL
  ASYNC_BOUNDARY: await
  TIMEOUT: timeout per target → TIMEOUT via ATTEMPT_DIAL and CLASSIFY_ERROR
  CANCELLATION: parent context cancel → in-flight probes observe cancelled ctx; POST partial results may remain ERROR or TIMEOUT
  SEQUENCING: AWAIT all workers before RETURN results
  MESSAGE_CONTRACT: N/A — no message/event delivery
  RETRY: N/A — single dial attempt per target
  IDEMPOTENCY: N/A — read-only probe per target
  DATA_TRANSITION: results[i] unset → Result after AWAIT worker i
  TERMINATION: bounded — all workers complete before RETURN

procedure RUN_ALL(): # [IMPL-TCP_CONNECT_PROBE] [ARCH-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER] [REQ-TCP_CONNECT_CHECKER]
1. results := allocate Result slice len(targets)
2. FOR each index i, target IN targets START worker:
   a. child_ctx := apply deadline timeout to parent context
   b. AWAIT ATTEMPT_DIAL(child_ctx, target, dialFn) into results[i]
3. AWAIT all workers complete
4. RETURN results
